questions.criteria:
1 mark per correct characteristic of difference, up to 2:
- size: the early bumblebee is small (and agile) whereas the garden bumblebee is larger;
- tongue: the garden bumblebee has a longer tongue (reaches deep flowers);
- agility: the early bumblebee is agile / can enter drooping flowers.

1 mark per point, up to 2:
- pollination enables plants to grow / plants can only grow because of it;
- it enables a plant to reproduce;
- it enables a plant to produce food;
- it keeps the cycle of a plant's life turning.

1 mark per developed point, up to 3:
- we enjoy a range of foods (orchard fruits, coffee, vanilla) thanks to bee pollination;
- we have cotton for clothing because cotton plants are pollinated;
- bees have been a fascinating subject of study/inspiration for poets, artists, authors and scientists (education/culture).

1 mark per valid inference based on paragraph 6, up to 3:
- pesticides make our food safer and more prolific, so people prioritise that benefit;
- people need/want to urbanise and build houses (housing comes first);
- intensive farming methods serve human demands;
- thoughtlessness/selfishness — people are unaware of, or ignore, the impact of their decisions on bees.
